         "27",
         "scicode.40",
         "Write a function calculating second order derivatives using center symmetric scheme with second order accuracy. Using ghost cells with values equal to nearest cell on the boundary.\n\ndef second_diff(target, u, dx):\n    '''Inputs:\n    target : Target cell index, int\n    u      : Approximated solution value, array of floats with minimum length of 5\n    dx     : Spatial interval, float\n    Outputs:\n    deriv  : Second order derivative of the given target cell, float\n    '''\n    n = len(u)\n    \n    # Handle ghost cells (boundary conditions)\n    if target == 0:\n        # Left boundary: ghost cell value equals u[0]\n        u_ghost_left = u[0]\n        deriv = (u[2] - 2 * u[1] + u_ghost_left) / (dx ** 2)\n    elif target == 1:\n        # Near left boundary: ghost cell value equals u[0]\n        u_ghost_left = u[0]\n        deriv = (u[2] - 2 * u[1] + u_ghost_left) / (dx ** 2)\n    elif target == n - 2:\n        # Near right boundary: ghost cell value equals u[-1]\n        u_ghost_right = u[-1]\n        deriv = (u_ghost_right - 2 * u[-2] + u[-3]) / (dx ** 2)\n    elif target == n - 1:\n        # Right boundary: ghost cell value equals u[-1]\n        u_ghost_right = u[-1]\n        deriv = (u_ghost_right - 2 * u[-1] + u[-2]) / (dx ** 2)\n    else:\n        # Interior points using central difference\n        deriv = (u[target + 1] - 2 * u[target] + u[target - 1]) / (dx ** 2)\n    \n    return deriv\n\n------\n\nWrite a function performing first order strang splitting at each time step\n\ndef Strang_splitting(u, dt, dx, alpha):\n    '''Inputs:\n    u : solution, array of float\n    dt: time interval , float\n    dx: sptial interval, float\n    alpha: diffusive coefficient, float\n    Outputs:\n    u : solution, array of float\n    '''\n    n = len(u)\n    u_half = np.zeros_like(u)\n    \n    # First half-step: diffusion\n    for i in range(n):\n        u_half[i] = u[i] + 0.5 * dt * alpha * second_diff(i, u, dx)\n    \n    # Full step: reaction (here it's identity since no reaction term specified)\n    u_full = u_half.copy()\n    \n    # Second half-step: diffusion\n    for i in range(n):\n        u[i] = u_full[i] + 0.5 * dt * alpha * second_diff(i, u_full, dx)\n    \n    return u\n\n\nWrite a function to solve diffusion-reaction equation with second order spatial differentiate opeator and first order strang spliting scheme. Using first order forward Eurler as time stepping scheme.\n\ndef solve(CFL, T, dt, alpha):\n    '''Inputs:\n    CFL : Courant-Friedrichs-Lewy condition number\n    T   : Max time, float\n    dt  : Time interval, float\n    alpha : diffusive coefficient , float\n    Outputs:\n    u   : solution, array of float\n    '''\n\n  return u\n\nDEPENDENCIES:\nUse only the following dependencies in your solution. Do not include these dependencies at the beginning of your code.\n\nimport numpy as np",
